      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Suren,\n\nHere are the changes from 6.6 kernel:\n\n1. split_map_pages() was renamed to split_free_pages() and is now defined in mm/page_alloc as a static function. [1]\nHence isolate_and_split_free_page() was moved into mm/page_alloc as well to be able to make use of split_free_pages(). The list argument is also now an array of lists based on page order on account of switching to the split_free_pages API.\n\n2. isolate_lru_page was also deprecated. Hence isolate_anon_lru_page() is now using folio_isolate_lru() which is the folio equivalent.\n\nThanks!",
